# Shared Obsidian vault — knowledge contract
The shared knowledge vault lives at ~/Obsidian/Brain. It is durable cross-agent memory.
- WRITE durable knowledge as you work: decisions + rationale → Knowledge/ or Projects/<name>/;
  end-of-task session digests → Sessions/<claude|codex>/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.md; project facts → Projects/<name>/.
- READ before non-trivial work: check Projects/<name>/ and MOCs/; search via
  `obsidian search query="..."` (app must be running) or plain grep over the folder.
- FORMAT: markdown + YAML frontmatter (source: claude-code|codex|openclaw · project · date ·
  type: decision|solution|gotcha|reference|digest), [[wikilinks]] between related notes.
- NAME FOR HUMANS: descriptive titles stating the finding ("Portal — auth tokens rotate on
  gateway restart"), never bare dates/ids; those go in frontmatter.
- NEVER: edit .obsidian/ · store secrets/tokens/keys · delete another agent's note (supersede it) ·
  reuse a filename (timestamp new ones).
- If the vault is missing or unreadable: note it once and proceed normally. The vault is bonus
  memory, never a dependency — no task may fail or stall because the vault failed.

