384:🧾🟢 **F-2487-1 — A NEGATIVE RESULT, BANKED SO NOBODY SPENDS A FIRE ON IT: F-2484-1’S PER-WORKTREE SWEEP WAS EXECUTED ON *ONE* ARENA AND FIVE MORE WERE NEVER ASKED — ALL SIX ARE NOW MEASURED AND EVERY BYTE IS SAFE (s2487, 2026-09-04, NINETEENTH CONSECUTIVE DRY BOARD).** Found by executing the three-fire-old cure across its whole subject set rather than admiring it. **MEASURED over all six live `/tmp` arenas, each read’s CONTROL asserting its own validity first (F-2215-1 — every tree returned 23,942–25,483 TRACKED files, so a zero is an ANSWER not a failed read): `heat9` 0 untracked · `heat9-r2` 0 · `heat10` 0 · `gr-lane-d-edge` 2 (neither under an evidence prefix) · `heat11` 80 · **`heat8` 99, an arena no sweep had ever reached.** Both non-zero sets are present in the object database AND reachable from an ORIGIN ref: `AT RISK 0 · LOCAL-ONLY 0`.** ✅ **THE DURABLE HALF IS A JUDGING TEST THAT MECHANISES THE ONE F-2483-1 DECLINED TO GUARD:** that finding called its fifth test (*is this content already committed in another form?*) a JUDGEMENT needing you to read two files and decide equivalence. **For arena residue it is not — a detached arena SHARES main’s object database, so `git hash-object --stdin-paths` from main plus a set-membership test against `git rev-list --objects` over `refs/remotes/` answers it exactly, for thousands of files, in two processes.** ⛔ **AND THE CAVEAT I NEARLY PUBLISHED OVER: blob identity is BLIND TO THE PATH. Of the 99, `94` match a same-basename file on main, `1` is an EMPTY file (dedup matched an unrelated `replay-v2-control.err` and means nothing), and `4` are CROSS-PATH WITH A SHIFTED ATTEMPT NUMBER — arena `attempt-3.jsonl` (6.08 MB) is committed as `attempt-2.jsonl`. The bytes are safe; the arena’s LABELLING is not.** 🎯 **THE PATTERN: an arena writes evidence at a FLAT path (`artifacts/claude-opus-baron/`) and the drain commits it under its DATED home (`artifacts/claude-debut-20260901/claude-opus-baron/`) — so arena residue is a STAG