492:✅ **F-WIN-2 — THE KIT-VS-BOSS GUARD HAS NO CODE FACT TO STAND ON, AND THAT IS AN OWNER RULING (lane-a 2026-09-02, drained s2457).** Split out of the lane's combined `F-WIN-1 / F-WIN-2` row so it carries its own declaring subject rather than riding inside another finding's (the F-1328-3 shape — caught by `desk-declaration-guard` in my own closing battery, F-1300-4). **F-WIN-1 is the RECEIPTS half and it SHIPPED**: 36 door contracts published where the task and spec say 39, `e1-drill-yard` admitted but rejected by `functions/api/standings.ts` (`practice.standings:false`) and so recorded `unclaimed / standings-disabled`. **F-WIN-2 is the GUARD half and it is PARKED, by the master's own honesty clause.** The requested invariant — *no contract may field a boss its starting kit cannot hurt* — cannot be expressed truthfully against today's runtime: `HeadlessContractSim.ts:819` says the Steamworks arsenal is not a floor or grant and a virgin profile leaves all three shooters disabled, `Game.ts:1563` gates them on research plus the Baron medal, yet `CombatSystem.ts:891` routes ordinary bolts into every live enemy and `Enemy.ts:774` gives the railcar no immunity. **So removing `twist.pressureEnabled` cannot make a literal "can damage" guard red, and the E2 mutation proof the master demanded has nothing to measure.** **GATE — attended ruling picks the invariant: (a)** add a real standalone pressure-arsenal floor in a separately scoped balance/grant slice and guard THAT, or **(b)** define "can hurt" as generic projectile damage and replace the mutation proof. **rec (b) first** — it is honest about what the runtime does today and costs one small slice; (a) is the larger design statement and can follow. **Do not encode `pressureEnabled` as an arsenal grant while the runtime says it is not one.** ⚖️ **Nothing is broken and nothing waits on this: the receipts half stands alone and shipped at `b5850417ad05b1e870d8fda8866a86f32bf400b1`.** Review: `reviews/winnability-receipts.md`