654:📰🕳️ **F-2410-1 — A COUNTY RIDE IS NEWS THAT CHANGES NO CODE, AND THE GZ-01 SWEEP CANNOT SEE ONE BY CONSTRUCTION (measured s2410; three live instances found and backfilled the same fire).** `gazette-backfill-sweep.mjs` selects its subject set on PATH (`PLAYER_PREFIXES` = `src/ assets/ public/ functions/ site/ index.html`), so a merge touching none of them is never examined. **A ride, a heat, a standing lands as `artifacts/` evidence plus a ledger row - no code - so NO path prefix can express it at ANY width.** 📊 MEASURED over 4,469 first-parent commits since 2026-08-05: of the 227 commits the outbox itself carries as REPORTED news, **76 (33.5%) touch no player path**. ⚠️ That figure is an UPPER BOUND and includes hashes cited incidentally in method notes - read it as evidence the class is real and large, NOT as a precise miss count. ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: this is NOT a false green.** The tool DECLARES its scan space on every run, in its own words - *"a merge touching NONE of these is never examined - widen the list, not the verdict"* - and `gazette-scan-space-guard` pins that list, so nothing lied. What earns it a finding is the DIRECTION at the one moment it fires: a dry-board fire reads `NOT cited anywhere - candidates to judge: 0` and reports GZ-01 DISCHARGED. 🎯 **THREE LIVE INSTANCES, every one confirmed uncited by direct grep across the WHOLE outbox before anything was claimed (the classifier and the hand-grep agreed): `40a2cc0c` (2026-08-23, the first standing ever verified end to end on the county's own iron), `c985a8d6` (2026-08-29, THE CROWN IS CLAIMED - the first machine-verified Baron admission), and `adec84db` + `9679303b` (the Claude debut one-two, rank 1 at 680g and rank 2 at 499g).** All backfilled to `gazette-queue.md` this fire at `621a7df12`, and the debut was verified against the LIVE county board rather than taken from our own record: `/api/standings?epoch=epoch-1-frontier&contract=the-claim` reads rank 1 `Claude Opus 5` 680g `verified`, rank 2 `Claude Fable 5` 499g `verified`, matching the ledger row for row. ⓘ The Baron item is reported with its own caveat rather than as fresh triumph: it was ridden under era 3, era 5 has since stepped every old crown down, and the era-4 re-earn was reported here at the time - so the owner was never left believing the Baron unbeaten. 💰 **THE CURE IS PRICED AND ITS KEY IS MEASURED, so the next fire inherits a job rather than a hunch. `artifacts/` is UNUSABLE as a bucket - 216 commits outside the subject set, 210 of them uncited, i.e. pure noise that would be excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1, the `cross-engine` fate). But a commit that ADDS a `*submission*.json` - a payload POSTED to the public board, so a county event BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by judgement - yields exactly 4 in 27 days, ALL FOUR uncited, and they are precisely the three instances above plus one correctly-dismissible retention mirror (`d2e75b81`, dismissed in the same commit).** rec: print that bucket as a THIRD declared advisory count beside `candidates`, WARN-level, never a red - F-1600-1 explicitly forbids mechanising player-visibility as a gate. 🚫 **DELIBERATELY NOT BUILT THIS FIRE, AND THE REASON IS MEASURED RATHER THAN A BUDGET EXCUSE: rooting its guard in `test:ledger-guards` edits `package.json`, which sits in `ENGINE_SOURCE_INPUTS` (`scripts/assay-replay-agent.mjs:36-48`, read by eye and not grepped; `package.json` is `:38`), so it would move the engine identity hash off `386f971d…` - the EXACT value F-2408-1's attended remedy is poised to pin.** Confirmed by reading `daae36dc7`, whose ENTIRE `package.json` delta is one guard filename appended to that chain, which is what moved the hash in the first place. **This cure must land AFTER the F-2408-1 ruling, or it stales the pin it is waiting on.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is F-2389-1's lesson one instrument over: F-2345-1 cured THIS SAME TOOL by WIDENING the path list (adding `site/`), and nobody then asked whether the AXIS can express the defect at all. It cannot - a ride is news because of what it RECORDS, not what it changes.** ⓘ And the knowledge already existed in this repo: the 08-30 ticker digest's own method note says a path filter *"would have missed"* the walking Baron, so the DIGEST COMPILER knew exactly what the SWEEP did not. **A fact recorded in a digest's prose is not a fact the instrument has** - this factory's most-repeated finding (F-2153-1 · F-2204-1 · F-2350-1 · F-2360-1 · F-2365-1) arriving on a new axis for the sixth time.
