752:✅ **F-SHOW-0830 — BOTH FORKS (a + b) ANSWERED by the owner 2026-08-30 AND FULLY SHIPPED; RETIRED FROM THE DESK s2467.** Verified INDEPENDENTLY of this row’s own body text, because a closure claim in a row body is not evidence: `specs/embodied-hand.md` is **Status: RATIFIED 2026-08-30** and quotes the owner verbatim — "yes, all of this. lets improve this" — ratifying (1) embodied BUILD, (2) the true reel renderer, (3) era rotation + crown re-earned. **Every slice of that spec has since MERGED**, so this is answered AND delivered rather than merely acknowledged: EH-1 `embodied-build-v2` @`a73790d9a2` (spec law 1, "one door, one hand" — a walking hand cannot anchor-build, which is what ABSORBS the 0830a static-play fork), EH-2 `true-reel-harness` @`8c5684def8`, EH-3 `true-reel-show` @`af85497537` (this IS 0830b option (ii), the true renderer the owner asked for by name: "can we not convert the AI tape to a human watchable tape?"), EH-4 `gauntlet-heat7-embodied-crown` @`b43df480f3`. ⚠️ **A word from Robin puts either fork back on the desk** — s2467 retired items he ANSWERED; it decided nothing for him. The closure was recorded in this row’s BODY on the day it was answered, where the subject-first rule correctly gives it no standing — see **F-2467-1**. Original triage preserved verbatim below. —— 🎭 **F-SHOW-0830 — THE OWNER WATCHED THE BARON CROWN REEL AND CALLED IT FAKE (owner 2026-08-30, verbatim: "it ended at 10 minutes, the AI never moved a single step, opponents walked into it and died in it. I think this is fake.").** TRIAGED honestly in three parts. ① THE RIDE IS REAL - forensics from the banked per-wave transcript (artifacts/baron-era3-20260829/run-1.jsonl): the hero is stationary by STRATEGY but piloted hard (30 level-up picks, SET_WEAPON blast/rig swaps, aimed BLAST_AT into the choke, REPAIR_UNDER; works took 7 wreckages and sat at 54% HP at the end; hero hit at w21-22; 985 kills by turret/beacon/blast fire); the assayer re-simulated from tick 0 and reprodu