772:🕳️🛠️ **F-2357-1 — MEASURED AND CURED s2357 `d2e75b815`: AN UNCITED, UNTRACKED EVIDENCE FILE UNDER `artifacts/` IS VISIBLE TO NEITHER OF THE TWO INSTRUMENTS THAT LOOK AT EVIDENCE, AND THE FACTORY HAS NO THIRD.** `artifacts/gauntlet-heat6-20260825/e1-baron/run-2-submission.json` sat in **no object database on any ref** — 464,284 B, never in history, not gitignored — while its `run-1` counterpart and all three of its own `run-2` siblings (`-tape.json`, `.jsonl`, `.stderr.log`) were tracked from the runner commit `00073a187`. 📊 **MEASURED REPO-WIDE, so the blast radius is a fact and not an impression: `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard` returns `47` untracked non-ignored files — `43` under `.claude/`, `2` under `logs/`, and **exactly ONE** under `artifacts/`.** 🔑 **THE GAP IS PRECISE AND BOTH INSTRUMENTS ARE CORRECT WITHIN THEIR DECLARED SCOPE, WHICH IS WHAT MAKES IT INVISIBLE RATHER THAN NEGLECTED — established by READING the corpus definitions, not by running them and inferring: `review-evidence-audit.mjs` DOES cover this directory (`EVIDENCE_PREFIXES = ['artifacts', 'reviews/shots-']`) but is **CITATION-DRIVEN** — it iterates backticked spans found in review files, so a path no review cites is never a subject, and it declares exactly this in its own output (*"a cited path outside these is not counted at all"*); `art-staging-audit.mjs` asks the untracked question but its scan set is *"every place ART-slot output is known to land"*, so `artifacts/` is outside it entirely — not even in its honest `NOT AUDITED` list, which names only the four unowned trees under `worktrees/`.** ➡️ **So the two live evidence instruments partition on ORTHOGONAL axes — one by CITATION, one by LOCATION — and a file that is both uncited and outside the art tree falls between them.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: realised cost is ZERO. One file, on disk the whole time, nothing lost, and it is the SECOND run of a contract whose `run-1` is tracked and is