r regression proving it.** Evidence: `tasks/runs/20260825-184236-lane-c-door-epic-envelope-v2.md.log` (report tail at `:73686`/`:74404`), mirrored at `logs/runs-archive/20260825-184236-lane-c-door-epic-envelope-v2.md.log`; `src/game/Game.ts:7244`; the `door-epic-envelope-v2` leaf `stopNote`; archive ref `archive/door-epic-envelope-v2-s2310-stopped-5645c5b9`. **GATE: OWNER RULING ON F-2299-2 (a) vs (b) — no re-author may be queued until that word lands, because every candidate master implements one side of the fork. PIPELINE-DRY for this thread.** ⚖️ **UPDATE (attended 2026-08-26): THE WORD LANDED - GATE LIFTED FOR THE SERVER SIDE ONLY.** Owner verbatim "Lets do this one here first", ruled on the attended storage-wall framing (row 1, this date) - words the fires could not see (chat, not ledger; recorded this commit). That authorizes the SERVER-SIDE envelope: `door-epic-envelope-v3` (lane-c) re-lands the archived `5645c5b91`, gating on both banked tapes verifying by the DIRECT door, which the browser ceiling never touches. **The (a)-vs-(b) PLAYER-PATH choice - omit `keepalive` above the ceiling vs keep-and-shrink - REMAINS on the desk**: the owner's word predates this measurement and names storage, not the submission path. PIPELINE-DRY now holds for the `Game.ts` keepalive edit ONLY. ✅ **ANSWERED (a) - owner 2026-08-26, verbatim: "yes, large runs have to be submittable as well for sure". PIPELINE-DRY FULLY lifted; `door-player-epic-submit` (lane-d) executes the runner's smallest fix. Thread status: server side = door-epic-envelope-v3 (lane-c), player side = door-player-epic-submit (lane-d), zero shared files.** Attended recommendation when he rules: (a) omit `keepalive` for oversized submits - a post-victory submit is a foreground act, and refusing a lawful epic at the county's own door contradicts the same-door law; (b) stays coherent only if compactness itself is meant to be part of the Baron's ask. ✅ **OWNER ANSWERED THE PLAYER-PATH FORK (2026-08-26):** "yes, large