 neither half of that sentence should be dropped. 🔺 **OWNER/ATTENDED-GATED DESIGN FORK (CLAUDE.md §7.3) — DO NOT RE-AUTHOR PRESUMING AN ANSWER:** raising the entry ceiling moves the recorder's own bound and the replay/DoS cost, while curing `gr-sim` to truncate honestly would make the Baron's win **unrecordable** — the opposite of the owner's intent. **RECOMMENDATION: do BOTH — treat the entry ceiling as the duration law's third sibling (per-contract, derived from the contract's own semantics + margin, exactly like `door-tick-ceiling-v2`), AND cure `gr-sim`'s hardcoded `truncated: null` so the harness stops asserting a completeness it did not check.** Either alone leaves the county either lying or the Baron locked out. ⓘ **THIS CORRECTS THE PREMISE OF A DESK ITEM ALREADY OPEN: 🔺 F-2299-2 reads *"Baron reel 464,285 B vs a 64 KiB ceiling"* and aims recommendations (b)/(a) at that ceiling — measurably the WRONG one. Re-read it before ruling; this finding does not add a 38th desk item, it re-points an existing one.** Evidence: `tasks/runs/20260825-142437-lane-c-door-reel-ceiling.md.log` (the lawful STOP), `artifacts/gauntlet-heat6-20260825/e1-baron/run-1-tape.json` and `run-2-tape.json` (`eventLogHash fnv1a32:2422a5fb`, `outcome.secured true`), the leaf `stopNote` on `door-reel-ceiling`, and F-2302-2 below (the pattern these three stops share).
