972:✅ **F-2291-1 MEASURED — THE BARON RE-SECURES ON TODAY’S ENGINE AND DOOR. F-2290-2’S OWED RUN IS DONE, AND IT REPRICES THE FORK IT WAS ASKED TO PRICE.** s2291 rode the retained Aug-13 player **byte-identically** (10,055 B, copy verified equal to the tracked file — the strategy was relocated, never edited) at engine `d020e5b46`, contract `e1-baron`, first pinned bench seed `e1-baron-01`: **`secured:true waves:22`**. 📊 **EIGHT OF NINE OUTCOME FIELDS REPRODUCE THE AUG-13 REPORT EXACTLY across a twelve-day engine gap** — `timeMs:596967 gold:319 kills:985 calls:3294 defaultedPicks:0 defaultedSecure:0`, every one identical. ⚖️ **SO THE RECOMMENDATION’S PREMISE IS NOW FALSE AS STATED:** (b) ACCEPTED-ELITE rests on *"eleven distinct current-door hypotheses remain 12.34× short"*, and F-2290-2 already noted it was silent about the twelfth. **The twelfth still works — today, on the current door, reproducibly.** The Baron is NOT an unbeatable wall for an agent; it is a wall exactly one known strategy clears. **This does NOT flip the admission and does NOT rule on the fork — s2290’s instruction is respected verbatim; the owner’s word is still owed, now against a measured board rather than a counted one.** 🌲 **THE PALISADE CAVEAT — RESOLVED BOTH WAYS, in the direction that KEEPS the strategy viable.** By code: `src/agent/MechanicsManifest.ts:693` puts `palisade` in `registryBuildables` **unconditionally** (the only filter on that list concerns turrets under `twist.powerGrid`). By the run: **3 palisades built, first at wave 19**, exactly as the plan specifies, final works `{sentry_beacon:6, palisade:3, sluice:3, stockpile:2, turret:4}` — the plan executed in full. **The palisade is a late decoy at wave ≥19, not a foundational affordance; AP-16 did not take it away.** 🔬 **DETERMINISM CONTROL RUN, not assumed:** a second identical ride returns an identical outcome **including the hash**, and the two tapes differ in **exactly one leaf** — `.id`, a `randomUUID` run identity (`scrip