1471:🔬 **F-2108-1 (s2108 2026-08-21, DRY BOARD — A DESK ROW'S HEADLINE WAS REFUTED ON MAIN SIXTEEN HOURS BEFORE THIS FIRE AND THE ROW STILL ASSERTS IT; ITS s2072 VERIFICATION HAS ROTTED IN BOTH HALVES; ITS ATTENDED-OWED GATE IS DISCHARGED TWICE OVER; AND WHAT SURVIVES IS THE SAME QUESTION AS TWO OTHER DESK ROWS THAT HAVE NEVER BEEN LINKED TO IT.)** 📋 **WHY THIS RUN EXISTED, AND THE METHOD IS s2107's.** s2107's priority (C) generalised its own win into a search: *"when a row predicts its own figure will rot and says nothing is watching, that sentence is a dated alarm — go set it off"*, and named the phrases to grep. I ran that grep across all 29 carried desk rows at the BACKLOG line numbers `desk-state-audit` resolves for each: **13 of 29 carry at least one alarm phrase.** Ranked by cost, the cheapest was **F-1608-2** at 2,014 chars, carrying both *"nobody has"* and *"silently"*. 🎯 **THE FIGURES IT FLAGGED ARE INTACT — AND THAT NEGATIVE RESULT IS WHAT AIMED THE REST OF THE FIRE.** F-1608-2's claim is that the Hill Mine Baron's `hpScale` was cut 30 → 12.5 while Trestle Run and The Incline retain 30, and it cites a count and two coordinates. **Re-measured on main: `hpScale": 30` returns exactly 2, at `assets/contracts/epoch-2-steamworks/contracts.json:418` and `:810`, the two coordinates the row names — no rot in count and none in coordinate**, and the hill mine sits at `12.5` at `:182`. ⓘ **HITS CONTROLLED BEFORE THEY WERE BELIEVED:** the four top-level contract ids sit at `:6` `e2-hill-mine`, `:270` `e2-trestle`, `:478` `e2-pressure-garden`, `:640` `e2-incline`, so `:418` is inside the trestle and `:810` inside the incline — the two maps the row names, confirmed by containment rather than assumed from order. 🔑 **SO THE ROT WAS NOT IN THE NUMBER — IT WAS IN THE SENTENCE NEXT TO IT.** F-1608-2's reassurance reads *"Both maps are currently door-de-listed **per F-E2S-3**, so nothing is blocked meanwhile"*, and that clause has a history: it was **VOID for ~15 hours** when