`); public-verb with the centre vault planted **wave 16 / wave 14** (`fnv1a32:77a015de` / `fnv1a32:9c5b06ec`); idle floors **wave 2 / wave 3** unsecured, so **Law 2 holds**. **THE ESCORT WAS NEVER THE OBSTACLE** — the train reached the basin ALIVE on every run that got that far, at full guard (240/240) and at the three-quarters left after a vault (180/180), and the ratified plant cost lands exactly (240→180, pool and ceiling together). **WHAT LOSES IT IS AUTHORED GROUND:** the claim stands at (0,12) — ON the north edge of `center-green-waypoint` (x −10..10, z −6..12), the only buildZone within 30wu of it — so every gun must be built SOUTH of the body it defends and there is no ground at all north of the hero; waves enter from BOTH the west and east edges; and half the roster is `feral_terraformer` (hpScale 1.7, buildingDamageScale 1.4) against turret/beacon caps of 4 and 6. Fifteen distinct plays were measured before this was called, and each delta is recorded in the prover's own comments so a later rider does not re-buy them (front-loading timber 16→10; blast upgrades over economy 16→11; economy over damage 16→12; damage over plating 16→13; turrets pulled in beside the beacons 17→11; the six beacons clustered ON the claim +1). So `e9-seed-run` enters `CONTRACT_ADMISSION_EXEMPTIONS` with a measured reason and a re-admit condition — the `e2-trestle`/`e6-showroom` shape — and **`scripts/door-admission-baseline.json` plus skill.md's door-contracts fence are deliberately UNCHANGED**. Bench seeds `-01`/`-02` are minted and KEPT (seeds are the comparability unit, not an admission claim: `e2-incline` and `e6-showroom` carry theirs the same way). **DOOR DATA:** 5 `harvestAnchors` along the road (contract + mask table, which the mask guard requires to deep-equal): one in the south yard, three in the centre ground the road crosses at the claim, one in the north basin — the far pair the first draft used sat 60wu out and starved the map (measured: wave 11 with 30 gold in hand because both live seams were the south pair). **GATES (Node 26.4.0):** tsc + build rc=0 · same-game audit 3/3 with pins moved and **ATTRIBUTED BY REVERT-AND-REPRODUCE** (anchors emptied reproduced 0/341/779/14 and 1134 rows EXACTLY; the exemption row alone reproduced 5/0/351/809/13; the manifest rule and the new verb each reproduced the baseline, i.e. move NOTHING) · door-ratchet + bench-seeds + skill.md fences + null-floor-anchors + mask-tables **41/41** · floors regenerated **53, `--check` clean, 0 secured:true**, and the ONLY line that moved is the git-derived `eraStamp` — every floor row byte-identical, which is itself the proof this slice moved no floor. **🔺 F-A8-1 (by design, stated not hidden):** `HeadlessContractSim` hands the caravan a FRESH EMPTY `TileStateStore`, so no bench run can inherit a plant and no planted run can leak into the next seed — that is the isolation the floors need, and it means the PERSISTENCE half of A8 is proven in the browser (`e2e/e9-seed-run-caravan.spec.ts`: staged mid-run → nothing on disk → committed at run end → born as `noSpawnZones` at the next birth → refused forever after), not headless. **🔺 F-A8-2 (cadence, cured):** the plant window is 40s because 15s FELL BETWEEN TURNS — a headless rider is handed a turn only when something changes, ~30s here, and a rider standing on the stake with the train beside it measured `planted=0`. A window a player can see and an agent cannot reach is not a choice. **🔺 F-A8-3 (truth, non-blocking):** the contract's `engineDependencies` still names `persistent-planting-consumer` as `missing` — now false. NOT edited here: `twist.persistentPlanting` remains in `DECLARED_INERT_PATHS` (`ContractFamilies.ts:1598`), which is what OBLIGES a non-empty declaration at all (`:1713`), and that file is outside this firewall. Same call the E7 census made for the Dead Band (F-E7DB-1). **🔺 F-A8-4 (OWNER FORK, OPEN):** re-admitting the Seed Run needs one of — (a) an authored `twist.secureWave` below 20 for this map, (b) a buildZone north of the claim or a `heroStart` stake moved inside the box, or (c) accept it as an elite map and leave the exemption standing. All three are contract data or a ruling; none is engine work. **RECOMMEND (c)** for now: the exemption is honest and the mechanic already earns its keep in the browser. **🔺 F-A8-5 (reach, MEASURED):** the board row is `unlock: "secured:e9-dome-basin"` and `reverifyStagedContractLaunch` clears a staged launch whose contract is locked, so a no-`?debug` launch aimed at the Seed Run lands back on The Claim today — asserted in the spec, not described. **Unlike the Dead Band's F-E7DB-2 this is a progression step, not a dead end:** Dome Basin is admitted, playable and secured by ordinary play. Four attempts to seed the unlocked half through storage all measured `unlocked:false` and NONE is left behind as a passing-looking workaround. **⚠️ TWO REDS, ATTRIBUTED NOT ABSORBED:** `e9-canal-stages` failed twice inside a four-spec invocation and passed **3/3 SOLO** on the same tree (load flake, the known class); `e9-arsenal:77` fails solo and is **PRE-EXISTING, PROVEN BY CONTROL** — reverting `src/game/Game.ts` to the base commit `d931958b3` (this slice's only shared browser-side file) reproduced the identical failure. It is NOT in `reviews/suite-red-inventory.md`, so it is recorded as newly-observed and owed an inventory row. A third, `worker-type-coverage`, is **ENVIRONMENTAL rather than a red**: it spawns the hardcoded `<cwd>/node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc` and this WORKTREE's `node_modules` carries no `typescript` (the repo root's does — which is why `npx tsc` and `npm run build` both resolve); it fails identically solo and this slice touches **zero** files under `functions/` (`git diff --name-only -- functions` is empty). **The first node-guards battery ran CONTENDED** — its own probe reported *2 concurrent batteries* and another builder's `run-node-guards.mjs` was genuinely alive — so it was re-run SOLO rather than trusted. **🔺 F-A8-6 (process, cost 40 minutes, reusable):** the obvious way to wait for that battery — `until ! pgrep -f "run-node-guards"; do sleep 20; done` — **CAN NEVER TERMINATE, because the waiting shell's own command line contains the pattern and `pgrep -f` matches full command lines.** The loop matches ITSELF, and every later "is the machine free?" probe using the same pattern then reads its own waiters as batteries — two live pids, plausible elapsed times, indistinguishable from a slow neighbour. Diagnosed only by PRINTING the matched command lines instead of trusting the count. Cure: match the script path (`pgrep -f "run-node-guards\.mjs"`, which a quoted-string waiter does not contain) or exclude self via `| grep -v $$`. **The same trap applies to any pgrep/pkill guard-loop in the factory's shell scripts.** Review `reviews/e9-seed-run.md`.
