1561:🟡 **A6 THE CROSSING AND THE PROBE BUILT — `e8-far-side` DOOR-READY, PROPOSED (2026-08-20, headless Opus-5 agent on `worktree-agent-a6-far-side`; NOT yet drained).** The ratified A6 design shipped on top of A4 exactly as the sheet ordered ("A4 builds it, A6 reuses"). **SUPPRESSION REUSE VERIFIED, NOT REBUILT — zero lines changed in `SignalSuppression.ts`:** booting far-side headless produced `now.signalSuppression {declared:true, drones:true, playbooks:true, relayChains:false}` on the first try, and `deriveMechanicsManifest` already emitted `signal_suppression` with `off:["drones","playbooks"]` — the A4 rule GENERALIZED with no new code, and the ABSENT `relayChains` key is correctly NOT suppressed (literal-false, honoured literally). **NEW: `src/systems/ProbeRecovery.ts`** — same shape as its A4 neighbour (private ctor + `create()` off the CONTRACT, one-way latch, refusal counters, presentation-stripped diagnostics), and **armed ONLY when `twist.probePlayback.trigger` AND ≥1 `probeRecoveryZones` are both declared**. That guard is the load-bearing line: F-1471-1 is the standing casualty of a declaration with no completion path pinning `objectiveAllowsSecure` false forever, so a trigger with no crater arms NOTHING (pinned in the new spec, all four combinations). **THE VERB:** `CONTEXT_ACTION action:'recover'`, targetless like `fund` — the world names the target. **THE LATCH:** both engines' `autoSecureWaveForRun` (`HeadlessContractSim:688`, `Game:5141`) plus both `objectiveAllowsSecure` sites, in the canyon-connect shape — surviving to wave 20 with the probe still buried does NOT secure. **THE PLAYBACK:** the E7 jack-board's own banked line, sourced from the new `E7_WRONG_NUMBER_FRAGMENT` export rather than re-typed, so the Far Side and the board below cannot drift; browser announces it under `THE EXCHANGE · RECOVERED` + float text at the crater, headless writes a one-time `probe-recovered` replay event and a `now.probeRecovery` row. Suit-only stays the existing `