and it is green:** `ACTIVE_TILE_ID === 'e1-twin-banks' && moveTarget.x >= minX && moveTarget.x <= maxX ? Math.sign(moveTarget.x - blocker.x) || this.avoidanceSide() : this.blockerSlideDirection('x', moveTarget)` — shipped `5c27a1b5c` (*runner(lane-c): f1441-2-crossings-keep-their-z*, 2026-08-04). 🔑 **Two differences from the failed deadband, both load-bearing: (1)** it is goal-relative to the **BLOCKER'S CENTRE** (`moveTarget.x - blocker.x`), which is *stable* as the enemy moves, where the F-1510-1 defect is enemy-relative (`moveTarget[axis] - position[axis]`) and therefore **flips mid-slide**; **(2)** it gates on **the goal lying inside the blocker's padded span** — the head-on geometry itself — rather than on a magnitude, which is the thing the deadband kept failing to detect. 💡 **The reusable lesson is the embarrassing one: this class of conflict had ALREADY been solved once in this very file by scoping on GEOMETRY, and the factory then spent a fire trying to solve it with a SCALAR. A master proposing a mechanism should be required to say why the existing mechanism for the same problem does not apply.** 📋 **SCOPE:** test whether generalising that branch off `ACTIVE_TILE_ID` (apply it to any blocker whose padded span contains the goal) greens both judges. **FORBIDS** reverting `531bd923a`, editing either e2e spec, and re-pinning `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs` (F-1441-3); **REQUIRES** `test:node-guards` (F-1460-1 path trigger — the diff touches `src/entities/`) and all four `Terrain.landmarkBlockers()` consumers (F-1510-2, via `grep -rl landmarkBlockers e2e/`). ⚠️ **NOT AUTHORED s1511 by choice, and the reason is the honest half:** choosing that consumer battery honestly is the larger part of the work, and `e1-twin-banks` may depend on tile-specific footprint geometry that does not generalise — a NEGATIVE result must be licensed again. **GATE: closes when one tree has `landmark-collision:68` AND `never-trap:88` green on both projects at `--workers=1`, or a measured negative result shows the centre-relative span gate does not generalise.** Related: [F-1510-1], [F-1511-1], [F-1511-3], [F-1441-2], [F-BW-10]. ✅ **AUTHORED + DISPATCHED s1512 as `tasks/lane-f1511-2-blocker-slide-geometry-gate.md` → lane-c — and the hypothesis was MEASURED GREEN FIRE-SIDE BEFORE the lane run was spent, because s1510 and s1511 had each already spent one on this thread.** Detached worktree `gate-s1512` at base `6d1810dbd`, external vite on scratch port **5199** (`strictPort`), `--workers=1`, both projects. **Isolated + controlled headline: baseline `landmark-collision:68` 2 FAILED (reproduced twice), treated 2 PASSED.** Full pair with `never-trap`: baseline **rc=1, 4 failed / 14 passed**; treated **rc=0, 18/18 passed**, reproduced twice. **`never-trap` 8/8 green on every arm.** `tsc` rc=0; `test:node-guards` rc=0 with **no Baron sim pin moved** (the F-1460-1 hazard, checked rather than assumed). 🔑 **WHY IT WORKS, read from the code:** inside the padded span the approach is head-on, so `Math.sign(moveTarget.x - blocker.x)` is ~0 and the `|| avoidanceSide()` fallback restores the stable go-around **scoped to that geometry**; outside the span `blockerSlideDirection()` still applies, so F-BW-10 stays cured. That is precisely the axis the deadband could not reach, because it asked about a MAGNITUDE. **A negative result is re-licensed in the master anyway** — the fire-side arm is a 2-line patch in a scratch worktree, and a runner disagreement would be worth more than the confirmation. Evidence: `docs/bench/f1512-1-blocker-slide-geometry-gate.md`. Related: [F-1512-1], [F-1512-2].
