2595:🔺 **F-1414-1 (s1414, VERIFIED AT SOURCE — the cause of F-1400-3, named at last: THE SECURE GATE WAITS FOR A STRING THE CONTRACT NEVER EMITS.)** The predecessor run named this cause; I did not inherit it, I read the code, and it holds in four links. **(1)** The grafted gate keys on the mere PRESENCE of a baron block — `autoSecureWaveForRun: () => this.manifest.twist.baron && !this.baronBeaten ? Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER : …` — so any contract with a truthy `twist.baron` can never auto-secure until `baronBeaten` flips. **(2)** `baronBeaten` flips on exactly one string: `if (event.type === "enemy_killed" && event.eliteKind === "baron") this.postBaronDefeat(event.at)`. **(3)** `e2-hill-mine` declares `bossKind: "railcar"`, `secureWave: 12`, `escortCount: 6` and a five-part `components` array, and `src/systems/WaveSystem.ts:866` spawns every part with `eliteKind: baron.bossKind ?? "railcar"` — so `"baron"` is **never emitted**. **(4)** Therefore `baronBeaten` can never become true, auto-secure is withheld forever, and the run overruns `secureWave: 12` into the ceiling at wave 15. ⚠️ **THE OBVIOUS ONE-LINE CURE IS WRONG AND MUST NOT BE APPLIED BLIND:** `bossRemaining === 0` alone OVER-FIRES, because `bossGroupId` is written by **five** systems — `WaveSystem.ts:880`, `SalvageClawBossSystem.ts:365`, `OldDiggerBossSystem.ts:428`, `HomemakerBossSystem.ts:388`, `DredgeQueenBossSystem.ts:390` — so keying on group-death alone would let an unrelated boss group’s last kill secure a baron contract. ✓ `degradeBossGroup` (`src/entities/pools.ts:732-745`) was read and IS sound: `remaining` excludes the killed enemy and counts only the living, so `remaining === 0` genuinely means the last component died. **REC: tie the kill to the contract’s OWN declared `bossKind` and require the group down; make 3a/3b/3c explicit rulings rather than assumptions.** **GATE: CURED when `f1414-1` lands with the canary red reproduced BEFORE it is proven green.**
