main, verified by ancestry, not by grepping commit messages — Mistake #16). `tasks/lane-drill-yard-affordances.md` is byte-identical to its own done-move. **The wiring is not owed; it exists and is DORMANT**, and s1446's "no master is queued for it" sent the next fire looking for work that had already landed. **Measured this fire on the raws themselves:** all three are 1254×1254 with **NO alpha channel and ZERO pixels below alpha 250**, sitting on a *painted* ground whose outer-ring RGB spread is **43,53,57 / 54,57,50 / 35,41,38** per channel. The one working precedent, `assets/raw/prop-baron-banner.png`, is the **same slot, same generator, same native 1254×1254** — but its border is **exactly `255,0,255`, spread `0,0,0`**, and it extracts to `assets/processed/prop-baron-banner.png` at 384×384 **RGBA**. One differing variable: the background. The consumer at `src/game/DrillYard.ts:363` builds `SpriteMaterial({transparent:true, alphaTest:0.04})` and `:365` **hides the procedural station geometry**, so it needs a cut-out; `scripts/extract-alpha.mjs` keys a **flat** chroma background by border flood-fill at `--tol 26`, and the measured spread is ~2× that with **no key colour to name at all**, while `--full-bleed` skips keying and would emit an **opaque ~3.4-unit parchment billboard per station — strictly worse than the placeholder that ships today.** 🎯 **ROOT CAUSE IS A CONTRACT MISMATCH, NOT A BAD RENDER:** the art request reused the **contract-plate convention** (full-bleed, magenta explicitly forbidden — entirely correct for `plate-contract-e1-drill-yard.png`, LEDGER row 69, which is drawn into a UI card) for three files the code consumes as **in-world sprites**. Nothing is wrong with the drawings; the ground under them is. **CURE QUEUED: `art-drill-yard-stations-keyed.md` (FIRE-AUTHORED s1447, ART slot), which PREFERS AN IMAGE-EDIT OVER A REGENERATION** — CLAUDE.md §8's consistency law, plus a sharper reason: **a from-scratch re-roll risks re-introducing the gallows read F-1445-4 rejected and two retakes cleared, and the effigy read `prop-straw-man-stand.png` only passed by carrying no head, face, limbs or anatomy.** Those properties are held by the current pixels. Acceptance is a **measured background property** (outer ring exactly `255,0,255`, spread `0,0,0`) precisely because *the thing that failed was a background property nobody measured*. Extraction stays **fire-side** (CLAUDE.md §8) and is firewalled OUT of the master: the drain extracts, gates, and wakes the dormant glob. **GATE: the three props render in a plain Drill Yard boot with the procedural placeholders hidden, and an e2e assertion exists that would notice a rename** (the coverage hole **F-1437-3** predicted at `reviews/lane-drill-yard-affordances.md:86` — the format mismatch measured here is that same hazard one layer deeper). ✅ **CLOSED — SHIPPED s1449 `e212cc5c`: THE PROPS ARE ON THE PLAYER'S SCREEN AND THE GATE ABOVE IS MET IN BOTH ITS CLAUSES.** Review `reviews/art-drill-yard-props-extracted.md`; LEDGER row 70; leaf `e1-drill-yard-stations-keyed` flipped `queued → merged`. Extraction was the single command the row predicted (`--key ff00ff --size 384`, 384 matched to the `prop-baron-banner.png` precedent), into the exact filenames the eager glob lists. Gated on **scratch port 5237** because lane-c ran `f1448-1` for the whole fire (Mistake #12): tsc clean · build **1.16 s** · new plain-boot `e2e/drill-yard-station-art.spec.ts` **2/2** desktop + 390px mobile, zero console errors · adjacent **by grep** (`drill-yard`, `drill-yard-manifest`, `cp01-charter-roundtrip`) **28/28** both projects · `gr-sim` **9/9** · node guards **36/36**. ⭐ **BOTH HALVES OF THE GATE ARE ANSWERED BY A MANUFACTURED RED, NOT A GREEN:** with the three PNGs moved out and nothing else changed, the spec goes **RED** with `stationArt` reading `Array []` — the exact dormant state — then restored byte-identical. That is also the *"would notice a rename"* clause, since a rename and an absence are the same event to a glob. The new `DrillYardDiagnostics.stationArt` is what makes it visible at all: **this defect class hid for two fires precisely because nothing could see it.** 🔺 **F-1449-1 — THE DRAIN FOUND A DEFECT THAT WOULD HAVE SHIPPED, AND IT IS A CLASS DEFECT IN THE KEYER.** The first extraction was correct by **every number the probe had** — corners `alpha=0`, transparent fraction matching each raw's own `#ff00ff` fraction to a tenth of a percent, **residual magenta 0** — and drew a **bright magenta halo around every prop in game**. Keying sets alpha 0 but **leaves the key colour in RGB**, and *the GPU does not consult alpha when it filters*: bilinear filtering and mipmaps average RGB across neighbouring texels, so `#ff00ff` under the transparency bleeds into every edge texel surviving `alphaTest` — worst on **thin features** (table legs, bell frame posts), where downscaling averages one real texel against several key texels. Measured: **100% of transparent pixels held key-magenta RGB**, including **3,982 / 1,540 / 1,755** that directly touch visible art. **The already-shipped `prop-baron-banner.png` carries the identical property (4,128), so the fault is `extract-alpha.mjs`, not this batch — fixed as a CLASS at `c29040e7`.** `bleedEdges()` propagates visible colour outward under the transparency to exhaustion and **never touches alpha**, so transparent/opaque/partial counts and subject bboxes are **identical before and after** — the cut-out is bit-for-bit the same shape; key-magenta under transparency **100% → 0%**. `despillSaturatedKey` could never have caught it: it skips transparent pixels *by design*, because it corrects spill **on** the art, not **under** it. ⭐ **THE REUSABLE LESSON: THE PROBE WAS NOT WRONG, ITS QUESTION WAS** — it asked whether magenta survived among the **visible** pixels and truthfully answered 0. **Looking is what caught it** (F-1446-1), exactly as at s1445 and s1446; three consecutive drains on this one batch have now been