5270:  - 🔺 **lane-baron-fort-solidity STOPPED s1439 — `100bafe73e2c90835bfa00ac996b64db414cd2ec` — F-BW-19 STAYS OPEN: the owner can still walk through the Baron's fortress walls.** Owner, gate walk 2026-08-03: *"I was also able to walk through its fortress walls."* The runner returned **STOP, not READY-FOR-GATES, and it is right to have done so** — the obvious fix was **measured and rejected** rather than shipped. A single full-body `fortified_far_bank` rectangle (`29.8 × 3.1`) made an enemy settle near `(6.675, -13.080)` against a target at `(0, -5.8)` with a **longest stationary run over 1,400 fixed ticks**; the honest component split (five palisades + two platforms) **still stalled**, ending near `(2.220, -13.080)` after 30 simulated seconds with a normal high-HP enemy oscillating around `(2.35, -13.01)`. Root cause reported: `ClaimJumperEnemy.resolveBlocker()` does **local collision response only**, and `BuildSystem.palisadeRoute()` supplies long-obstacle waypoints for **player-built palisades only**, so static landmark blockers never enter the route graph — short bodies route acceptably, a continuous fort wall does not. Shipping the registry entries alone would have traded a walk-through wall for a **permanent enemy stall**, i.e. **MQ-3 "solid AND never-trap" failing on its second clause**. **Landed: `artifacts/fort-solidity/STOP-report.md` ONLY — 1 file, 36 insertions, ZERO code** (banked per the RETENTION LAW rather than left to die in the lane), carrying the **five-map E1 landmark solidity census**, four identified registry gaps (`active_headframe` on The Claim; `fortified_far_bank`, `seized_headframe`, `siege_line` on Baron) and honest footprints measured from the mounted bodies. Review `reviews/lane-baron-fort-solidity.md`. ⚠️ **F-1439-4 — the master asked for something a lane runner CANNOT do.** Scope 3 said *"coordinate with the stall-census tasks; run their probe if landed"*, and the STOP blocks on *"the repository has no landed stall-census probe to r