us hash moved and the sim did not drift between the two drains. **Gates: tsc 0 · build green 1.08 s · `agent-view` 10 passed = 5 desktop + 5 mobile (the derived 4+1) · adjacent `agent-seat`+`m4-10`+`er01-e2-census` 13 passed/1 skipped (the skip is `agent-seat` mobile, pre-existing) · `test:node-guards` rc=0, 354 tests/351 pass/0 fail/3 skipped with the pinned E2 Baron test PASSING and UNMOVED · plain-boot probe with NO `?debug` at 1280×800 and 390×844 = 0 console/page errors** (`reviews/shots-f1526-1/`, driver mirrored to `logs/runs-archive/s1528-gate-driver-boot-probe.mjs` per the RETENTION LAW, run on scratch port 5234 so a live lane could not contaminate it). Merge classification: both files **LANE-TOUCHED only**, `git log 2a3bfe39..main` over them **EMPTY** — no graft; a real `merge --no-ff` in the detached `gate-s1528` produced blobs **byte-identical to `lane/b`** (`ab970be9`, `b73ac06d`), proving the path-scoped application on main is the tree the battery ran against. 🔺 **Three non-blocking findings. F-1528-1:** the byte-stable wave-3 snapshot **MASKS** the new field as `"<point>"` rather than pinning it, so the strongest test in the file now asserts the field's presence and JSON position but **never its value** — coverage is not lost (the new dedicated test checks the value) but *a masked field in a change-detector is a field that detector can no longer detect changing.* **F-1528-2:** the runner **edited an existing test**, which the firewall NO list forbids in letter — **judged unavoidable and correct**, since growing the `now` type necessarily breaks a byte-stable snapshot OF the `now` type, so the choices were *edit the fixture* or *STOP and ship nothing*; the lesson is that the next master of this shape should carve the exception out **up front**, because a firewall forbidding the edit its own scope requires will either be violated or will stop the work. **F-1528-3 (informational, and it NARROWS AN OPEN OWNER FORK):** the headless **Prospector moves while